The evidence supports a precise caveat for question 3: removing the database-level cascade would make direct parent deletion with child rows fail, but this application’s two user-delete paths already avoid that (ORM relationship cascade or explicit `DELETE FROM item`). Therefore no current test function actually detects the specific `ondelete` regression; I’ll document the nearest tests and why they are insufficient.
